      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m a bit confused about what this `arrayLength()` call means now. It\u0027s being called on the result of the pointer offset (after the offset is applied and after the type is changed to `array\u003cu32\u003e`), but you\u0027re treating the result as if it will return the byte length of the original buffer?\n\nMaybe this is an argument for changing the buffer type to be `array\u003cu8\u003e` as you suggested in a different comment, and then this could become an `arrayLength()` called on the original variable instead? Otherwise I think you\u0027d have to also change the `ArrayLengthFromUniform` polyfill to skip over the pointer offset call (which is hard because that\u0027s a core transform not an MSL one).",
